Jervis Bay Marine Park
Jervis Bay Marine Park is a marine protected area established by the Government of New South Wales   in 1998. and the current zoning plan has been in place since 1 October 2002. The marine park is approximately 210 km2 (81 mi2) in area and spans over 100 km (62 mi) of coastline from Kinghorn Point in the north to Sussex Inlet.  The marine park is zoned to conserve biological diversity in marine habitats and to provide a range of recreational and commercial activities.


